name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-postassessment-q11_2025'

question 'A weather app uses one piece of code to display the forecast for any city a user searches for. Each time a user types a new city name, that name is sent into the same forecast function. What makes this possible?'

right 'The function uses a parameter to take in the city name and use it in its calculations.'
wrong 'The app creates a new copy of the same code for every city in the world.'
wrong 'The app saves each city name inside the HTML so the page never changes.'
wrong 'The function runs without needing any information from the user.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

